<template><article class="legal-page"><span class="eyebrow">NINTH / LEGAL</span><h1>{{type==='privacy'?'Privacy Policy':'Terms of Service'}}</h1><p class="updated">Foundation draft · August 21, 2026</p><section v-if="type==='privacy'"><h2>Account and analytical data</h2><p>NINTH stores account identity, authentication methods, revocable sessions, preferences and user-owned saved content. Platform game data and global model forecasts remain separate from private user records.</p><h2>Security</h2><p>Passwords are hashed with Argon2id. Session, verification and reset credentials are not stored as raw tokens. Sensitive credentials are never returned through the account API.</p><h2>Service providers</h2><p>PostgreSQL stores application records. Google may provide identity information only when you choose Google Sign-In. An SMTP provider delivers account-security messages.</p></section><section v-else><h2>Analytical purpose</h2><p>NINTH provides sports-analysis and model decision-support tools. Forecasts are probabilistic, are not guarantees and should not be treated as financial advice.</p><h2>Account responsibility</h2><p>You are responsible for maintaining access to your sign-in methods and for activity performed through your account. NINTH may revoke sessions that appear compromised.</p><h2>Saved content</h2><p>Saved predictions and builders retain model-version and generation context where available so historical outputs are not silently rewritten when models change.</p></section></article></template>
